# Donna, run locally (README.md, "Run Donna locally").
# Copy to .env and fill in. `npm run local:runtime`, `npm run local:web` and
# `npm run demo:fi` all read this file. A line starting with # is off; remove
# the # to set it. Never commit .env.

# ── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The key you type on the sign-in screen. The runtime refuses firm data
# without it. Any long random string, e.g. from `openssl rand -hex 24`.
DONNA_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Model providers (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without keys Donna starts, shows the demo company and stores uploads, but
# reads no document. With a key, the contents of documents and of the books
# are sent to that provider. At start the runtime prints which lanes are lit.

# Anthropic: every model task — document routing and reading (receipts,
# invoices, the bank statement), coding, ask drafting, reconciliation
# triage, bank-line disposition, chat, memory. One Anthropic key is enough.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OpenAI (optional): the same tasks, used only when no Anthropic key is set.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Typesafe (api.typesafe.ai): the first-line decisions for matching, bank and
# document disposition and coding. A local book stages this lane for every
# company it creates; without both values bank lines stay "Stalled".
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=
# Without a Typesafe key, switch that lane off instead so Claude codes the
# bank lines. This can only switch capabilities off.
# CLIENT_CONFIG_FORCE_DISABLE=JEV_RECONCILIATION
# Override the model id. Leave unset to use each task's own default model
# (claude-opus-5-5 on Anthropic). OPENAI_MODEL is also the coding, ask,
# chat and memory tasks' knob: a claude-* id there pins those on Anthropic,
# a gpt-* id pins them on OpenAI.
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# LOUIS_MODEL=
# Shadow challenger (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint). Records evidence only;
# runs only when all four are set.
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_MODEL=
# MODEL_CHALLENGER_CAP_TOKENS=

# ── Local runtime (optional; each comment gives the default) ──────────────

# Where the database, uploaded documents, backups and logs live.
# Default: ~/.donna-desktop
# DONNA_DESKTOP_DATA_DIR=
# Port of the runtime API on 127.0.0.1. Default: 8787
# DONNA_DESKTOP_PORT=
# Port of the web app on 127.0.0.1. Default: 5173
# DONNA_LOCAL_WEB_PORT=
# Postgres 16 bin directory (holds pg_ctl and initdb). Default: looked up in
# the usual install paths (/usr/lib/postgresql/16/bin, Homebrew, Postgres.app).
# PG_BIN=
# Suffix of the private Postgres socket; change only to run two books at
# once. Default: 5433
# DONNA_DESKTOP_PG_PORT=
# Uploaded documents. Default: <data dir>/documents
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BLOB_DIR=
# Backup packages. Default: <data dir>/backups
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BACKUP_DIR=
# When the daily backup runs (a cron expression) and how many to keep.
# Default: 30 1 * * * and 14
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BACKUP_CRON=
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BACKUP_KEEP=
# Set to off to run the API without background jobs (diagnostics only).
# DONNA_DESKTOP_SCHEDULER=
